{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Anneal",
    "version": "2.0.0",
    "description": "Music, speech and image generation running locally on a Mac mini M4, reachable over the tailnet.\n\nNamed for what it does to its models: heat one up on demand, let it cool and release the memory when idle.\n\n## Memory model — read this first\n\nThe host has 16 GB of unified memory. The music model holds ~21 GB once loaded and the image model ~11 GB, so **models are loaded on demand and unloaded after an idle period**, and the two heavy models are never resident at the same time — requesting one evicts the other. Music exceeds physical RAM on its own and therefore always swaps, which is why generation takes minutes rather than seconds.\n\nWhat that means for you:\n\n- A request against a cold model takes **3–4 minutes longer** while weights load. Set client timeouts to **900s or more**; a 30s default will fail every cold request.\n- Do not auto-retry a slow first request. A retry queues more work behind the one already running.\n- Call `POST /supervisor/start` ahead of time to pre-warm, or `GET /supervisor/status` to see what is currently loaded.\n- `GET /health`, `GET /supervisor/status` and `GET /v1/audio` never wake a model, so they are free to poll.\n\n## Auth\n\nEvery endpoint except `/health`, `/supervisor/status`, `/openapi.json` and `/docs` requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.\n\n## Concurrency\n\nOne job at a time per service. Music has a queue (max 200) that is held in memory and lost on restart — own your job state and be ready to resubmit."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://jons-mac-mini.pangolin-darter.ts.net",
      "description": "Tailnet (TLS)"
    },
    {
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8001",
      "description": "On the host itself"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "music",
      "description": "ACE-Step 1.5 — text to music with vocals. Asynchronous: submit, poll, download."
    },
    {
      "name": "speech",
      "description": "Kokoro-82M — text to speech. Synchronous, a couple of seconds."
    },
    {
      "name": "image",
      "description": "FLUX.1-schnell 4-bit — text to image. Synchronous, roughly two minutes per 1024px image."
    },
    {
      "name": "supervisor",
      "description": "Model lifecycle: what is loaded, pre-warm, unload."
    },
    {
      "name": "library",
      "description": "Everything generated, kept on disk and browsable. Never wakes a model."
    },
    {
      "name": "text",
      "description": "Gemma 4 e4b (4-bit) via mlx-lm — OpenAI-compatible chat completions, with streaming."
    },
    {
      "name": "press",
      "description": "One brief to a finished single or album: plan, lyrics, music and cover."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/release_task": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "music"
        ],
        "summary": "Submit a music generation job",
        "description": "Returns immediately with a task_id. Poll /query_result until status is 1 or 2.\n\nOnly `prompt` is required; anything omitted is filled in by a small planning LM.\n\n**Anneal applies two defaults that differ from the upstream backend**, because both materially affect output quality and every integrator would otherwise rediscover them:\n\n- `thinking` defaults to **true** (upstream: false). Runs the planning pass that decides sections, key and arrangement before any audio exists. Costs ~30s; without it structure is noticeably weaker.\n- `audio_format` defaults to **flac** (lossless). The backend's MP3 encoder is fixed at 128 kbps with no bitrate control, which is audibly lossy.\n\nSend either field explicitly to override.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MusicRequest"
              },
              "examples": {
                "instrumental": {
                  "summary": "30s instrumental",
                  "value": {
                    "prompt": "warm lo-fi hip hop with rhodes piano and vinyl crackle",
                    "lyrics": "[instrumental]",
                    "audio_duration": 30
                  }
                },
                "song": {
                  "summary": "Song with vocals",
                  "value": {
                    "prompt": "warm indie pop ballad, female vocals, brushed drums",
                    "lyrics": "[verse]\nStreetlights blur into the rain\n\n[chorus]\nHold on, hold on",
                    "audio_duration": 45,
                    "audio_format": "mp3"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Job accepted",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "allOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Envelope"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "object",
                      "properties": {
                        "data": {
                          "type": "object",
                          "properties": {
                            "task_id": {
                              "type": "string"
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "task_id": "42f580bc-f8a5-44c2-9685-a124f54d6f49"
                  },
                  "code": 200,
                  "error": null
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BackendUnavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/query_result": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "music"
        ],
        "summary": "Poll one or more music jobs",
        "description": "Poll every 3–5 seconds. There is no webhook.\n\n**`result` is a JSON-encoded string, not an object** — parse it a second time. It decodes to a list with one entry per take.\n\n**Jobs survive a restart.** The gateway records every job and replays anything outstanding when the backend restarts. Keep polling the id you were given — the replayed job gets a new id internally and the gateway translates both ways, so you will see `status: 0` across a restart and the result when it lands.\n\n**Orphaned jobs** are the residual case: something too old to replay, or that has failed repeatedly, returns `status: 2` with `\"orphaned\": true`. That is final — resubmit.\n\n**Transient errors.** A `502` during polling means the backend was restarting, not that the job failed. Retry the poll; never resubmit on a 502, or you will queue duplicate work.\n\n**Progress.** While a job runs, the decoded `result` carries `progress` (0.0-1.0) and a human-readable `stage` such as \"Generating music (batch size: 1)...\" or \"Decoding audio...\". Show these — a generation takes minutes, and without them a caller cannot tell slow from hung.\n\n**`metas` is intent, not measurement.** `bpm`, `keyscale` and `timesignature` are what the planning LM asked the DiT for, not an analysis of the audio produced. The LM can emit values plainly at odds with the result — 300 bpm for a folk ballad has been observed — while the audio itself is fine. Label them as requested values in any UI, or set `bpm`/`key_scale` explicitly on the request to remove the guesswork.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "task_id_list"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "task_id_list": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "task_id_list": [
                  "42f580bc-f8a5-44c2-9685-a124f54d6f49"
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Job states",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": [
                    {
                      "task_id": "42f580bc-...",
                      "status": 1,
                      "result": "[{\"file\": \"/v1/audio?path=%2FVolumes%2F...\", \"metas\": {\"bpm\": 96, \"duration\": 45}, \"seed_value\": \"12345\"}]"
                    }
                  ],
                  "code": 200,
                  "error": null
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/audio": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "music"
        ],
        "summary": "Download generated music",
        "description": "Served straight off disk by the gateway — this never wakes the music model.\n\n**Do not build this URL yourself.** The `file` field in a result is *already* a complete request path including its query string, e.g. `/v1/audio?path=%2FVolumes%2F...`. Append it to the base URL exactly as given:\n\n```\nGET {base_url}{file}\n```\n\nURL-encoding `file` and passing it as `path` double-encodes it. That used to fail with a misleading `403 Access denied`; it now returns `400` naming the mistake.\n\nFiles live in a cache the server prunes. **Persist the bytes yourself**; do not treat the URL as durable.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "path",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Absolute filesystem path, already URL-encoded inside the `file` field. You normally never set this by hand — just append `file` to the base URL."
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Audio bytes",
            "content": {
              "audio/mpeg": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "binary"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "File no longer exists"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/stats": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "music"
        ],
        "summary": "Queue depth",
        "description": "Wakes the music service. Use for backpressure or to show queue position.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Queue state",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "jobs": {
                      "total": 4,
                      "queued": 0,
                      "running": 1,
                      "succeeded": 3,
                      "failed": 0
                    },
                    "queue_size": 0,
                    "avg_job_seconds": 151.9
                  },
                  "code": 200
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/audio/speech": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "speech"
        ],
        "summary": "Synthesize speech",
        "description": "Synchronous — returns audio bytes directly. About 1–2 seconds per sentence once warm.\n\nKokoro is small enough that it can stay loaded alongside a heavy model.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SpeechRequest"
              },
              "example": {
                "input": "The local speech service is running entirely on device.",
                "voice": "bf_emma",
                "response_format": "mp3",
                "speed": 1.0
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Audio bytes",
            "content": {
              "audio/wav": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "binary"
                }
              },
              "audio/mpeg": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "binary"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Missing input, unknown voice, or unsupported format"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/voices": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "speech"
        ],
        "summary": "List available voices",
        "description": "Voice ids encode language and gender: `a`=American, `b`=British; `f`=female, `m`=male.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Voice ids",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "voices": [
                      "af_heart",
                      "af_bella",
                      "am_michael",
                      "bf_emma",
                      "bm_george"
                    ],
                    "default": "af_heart"
                  },
                  "code": 200
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/images/generations": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "image"
        ],
        "summary": "Generate an image",
        "description": "Synchronous. Measured at ~120s per 1024x1024 image at 4 steps on this hardware, plus ~30-60s model load if the image model is cold. Smaller sizes are proportionally faster.\n\nOnly one heavy model fits in memory, so an image request evicts an **idle** music model. If music is mid-generation the request is refused with **409** and a `Retry-After` header rather than killing that job — retry when it finishes, or stop music explicitly to take the slot. Set client timeouts to 900s or more.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ImageRequest"
              },
              "example": {
                "prompt": "a puffin standing on a mossy cliff at golden hour, photographic",
                "size": "1024x1024",
                "steps": 4,
                "n": 1,
                "response_format": "b64_json"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Generated images",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "created": 1785881567,
                  "data": [
                    {
                      "path": "/Volumes/Storage/AIMusic/outputs/images/a_puffin-42.png",
                      "url": "/v1/images/file?path=...",
                      "seed": 42,
                      "seconds": 34.2,
                      "b64_json": "iVBORw0KGgo..."
                    }
                  ],
                  "code": 200
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Missing prompt or invalid size"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "409": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/HeavyServiceBusy"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BackendUnavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/images/file": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "image"
        ],
        "summary": "Download a generated image",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "path",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "PNG bytes",
            "content": {
              "image/png": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "binary"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/health": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "supervisor"
        ],
        "summary": "Gateway and service state",
        "description": "Never wakes a model. Safe to poll as often as you like. No auth required.\n\nThe `system` block reports `free_mb`, `swap_used_mb`, `pageouts_per_sec` and `pressure_level` (macOS's own verdict: normal / warning / critical), plus a boolean `pressure`.\n\n**Do not treat swap volume as a problem.** This host routinely runs a model larger than physical RAM; macOS pages it out once and then idles at a negligible pageout rate. `pressure` is true only when the kernel reports warning or critical, or paging is genuinely sustained.",
        "security": [],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Per-service state",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "supervisor": "ok",
                    "services": {
                      "music": {
                        "running": false,
                        "heavy": true,
                        "idle_seconds": 812.4
                      },
                      "speech": {
                        "running": true,
                        "heavy": false
                      },
                      "image": {
                        "running": false,
                        "heavy": true
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "code": 200
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/supervisor/status": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "supervisor"
        ],
        "summary": "Detailed lifecycle state",
        "description": "Per-service RSS, peak RSS, idle seconds, in-flight count. Never wakes a model. No auth required.",
        "security": [],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Service detail"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/supervisor/start": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "supervisor"
        ],
        "summary": "Pre-warm a model",
        "description": "Blocks until the model is loaded and ready, then returns. Call this when you know work is coming so the user does not absorb the cold start.\n\nStarting a heavy service stops the other heavy service.",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "service": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "music",
                      "speech",
                      "image"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "service": "music"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Ready"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BackendUnavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/supervisor/stop": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "supervisor"
        ],
        "summary": "Unload now and free memory",
        "description": "Omit `service` to stop everything.",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "service": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "music",
                      "speech",
                      "image"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Stopped"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/outputs": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "library"
        ],
        "summary": "List saved outputs",
        "description": "Everything the server has kept, newest first. Reads the filesystem — no model is woken.\n\nEach item carries the prompt and the parameters that produced it, from a JSON sidecar written alongside the file.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "kind",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "music",
                "speech",
                "images"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "limit",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer",
              "default": 200,
              "maximum": 1000
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "offset",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer",
              "default": 0
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Saved outputs",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "total": 7,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "path": "/Volumes/Storage/AIMusic/outputs/music/2026-08-06T11-39-53_bright-acoustic-folk_28db5d.mp3",
                        "name": "2026-08-06T11-39-53_bright-acoustic-folk_28db5d.mp3",
                        "kind": "music",
                        "bytes": 321069,
                        "created": 1786012793.98,
                        "prompt": "bright acoustic folk with mandolin",
                        "meta": {
                          "bpm": 70,
                          "duration": 20.0,
                          "key_scale": "C minor",
                          "seed": "1984467799"
                        },
                        "url": "/v1/outputs/file?path=..."
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "code": 200
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "tags": [
          "library"
        ],
        "summary": "Delete a saved output",
        "description": "Removes the file and its sidecar. Refuses anything outside the outputs directory.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "path",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Deleted"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found, or outside outputs/"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/outputs/file": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "library"
        ],
        "summary": "Download a saved output",
        "description": "Serves any kind — audio or image — straight off disk. Never wakes a model.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "path",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "File bytes"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Not found"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/music/tiers": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "music"
        ],
        "summary": "List music quality tiers",
        "description": "Which model each tier uses, whether it is loaded, and whether it is usable at all. Answered by the gateway — never wakes a model. Check `available` before offering a tier: one is currently unusable for reasons outside Anneal's control, and `unavailable_reason` explains why.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Tiers",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "default": "draft",
                    "loaded_model": "acestep-v15-turbo",
                    "tiers": {
                      "draft": {
                        "model": "acestep-v15-turbo",
                        "steps": 8,
                        "label": "Draft — fast, distilled (8 steps)",
                        "loaded": true
                      },
                      "high": {
                        "model": "acestep-v15-sft",
                        "steps": 32,
                        "label": "High — fine-tuned, more detail (32 steps)",
                        "loaded": false
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "code": 200
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/chat/completions": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "text"
        ],
        "summary": "Chat completion (OpenAI-compatible, streaming supported)",
        "description": "Local Gemma 4 e4b. Standard OpenAI chat-completions shape, so most client libraries work by changing the base URL.\n\n**Streaming works** — set `stream: true` and the gateway relays SSE chunks as they arrive rather than buffering the completion.\n\n**This is a reasoning model.** By default it emits a long `delta.reasoning` channel before any `delta.content`, and will exhaust a small `max_tokens` while still thinking. For direct answers send `chat_template_kwargs: {\"enable_thinking\": false}`. Leave it on when you actually want the reasoning.\n\n`model` is ignored — the gateway substitutes whichever model is loaded, so you can send anything or omit it.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "example": {
                "model": "gemma",
                "stream": true,
                "max_tokens": 700,
                "chat_template_kwargs": {
                  "enable_thinking": false
                },
                "messages": [
                  {
                    "role": "user",
                    "content": "Write a verse of an indie folk song about waiting."
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Completion, or an SSE stream when `stream: true`"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BackendUnavailable"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/text": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "text"
        ],
        "summary": "Generate text (simple contract)",
        "description": "Prompt in, text out — for callers who don't want the OpenAI message shape.\n\nReasoning is **off** by default (Gemma 4 would otherwise spend a short token budget thinking before answering). Set `thinking: true` to keep it, or use `/v1/chat/completions` for full control and streaming.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "prompt"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "prompt": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "system": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Optional system message."
                  },
                  "max_tokens": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "default": 800,
                    "maximum": 4096
                  },
                  "temperature": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "default": 0.8
                  },
                  "thinking": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": false
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "prompt": "Name three moods for a rainy-day playlist."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Generated text",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "example": {
                  "data": {
                    "text": "1. Melancholy reflection.\n2. Cozy introspection.\n3. Dramatic yearning.",
                    "model": "mlx-community/gemma-4-e4b-it-4bit",
                    "usage": {
                      "prompt_tokens": 23,
                      "completion_tokens": 20
                    }
                  },
                  "code": 200,
                  "error": null
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Missing prompt"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/press": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "press"
        ],
        "summary": "Start a press",
        "description": "Returns immediately with a press_id; poll GET /v1/press?id=.\n\nRuns minutes to tens of minutes. Stages are ordered plan → all lyrics → all music → cover so each heavy model loads once. On an album, track lengths vary around `duration` rather than being uniform.",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "prompt"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "prompt": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The brief."
                  },
                  "tracks": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "default": 1,
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 8,
                    "description": "1 = single."
                  },
                  "duration": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "default": 90,
                    "description": "Nominal seconds; albums vary around it."
                  },
                  "duration_min": {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "duration_max": {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  "quality": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "draft",
                      "high"
                    ],
                    "default": "draft"
                  },
                  "instrumental": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": false
                  },
                  "art": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "default": true
                  },
                  "art_size": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "default": "1024x1024"
                  }
                }
              },
              "example": {
                "prompt": "a short winter album about leaving a coastal town",
                "tracks": 4,
                "duration": 90
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Started"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Missing prompt"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      },
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "press"
        ],
        "summary": "Press state, or recent presses",
        "description": "With `id`, the full record: plan, artist, per-track state, lyrics and cover. Without, recent presses.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Press state"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No such press"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/press/download": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "press"
        ],
        "summary": "Download a press as a zip",
        "description": "Audio, cover and tracklist in one archive. Masters are FLAC, so mp3/aac are transcoded from the lossless original rather than from another lossy copy.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "format",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "flac",
                "mp3",
                "aac",
                "wav"
              ],
              "default": "flac"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "bitrate",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "default": "320k"
            },
            "description": "mp3/aac only."
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Zip archive"
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Nothing finished yet"
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Unsupported format"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "bearerAuth": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "description": "Ask the host owner for the key. Read it from an env var; never commit it."
      }
    },
    "responses": {
      "Unauthorized": {
        "description": "Missing or invalid Authorization header"
      },
      "HeavyServiceBusy": {
        "description": "The other heavy model is mid-generation and will not be evicted. Nothing is broken — wait and retry (see `Retry-After`), or stop the busy service to claim the slot.",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "example": {
              "code": 409,
              "error": "music is mid-generation and only one heavy model fits in memory...",
              "busy_service": "music",
              "requested_service": "image"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "BackendUnavailable": {
        "description": "Model could not be started. `reason: host_memory_exhausted` means Anneal refused to load it because the machine is out of RAM — the body carries free/swap figures. Otherwise the backend failed to start, usually because the external SSD is unmounted on the host."
      }
    },
    "schemas": {
      "Envelope": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Every music and supervisor endpoint wraps its payload like this. Check `code == 200` — an HTTP 200 can still carry `code: 500`.",
        "properties": {
          "data": {},
          "code": {
            "type": "integer",
            "example": 200
          },
          "error": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "timestamp": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "milliseconds"
          }
        }
      },
      "MusicRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "prompt"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "prompt": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Style description: genre, instruments, mood, production."
          },
          "lyrics": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "",
            "description": "Use [verse] / [chorus] / [bridge] tags. Use \"[instrumental]\" for no vocals."
          },
          "audio_duration": {
            "type": "number",
            "minimum": 10,
            "maximum": 600,
            "description": "Seconds. Defaults to the model's choice."
          },
          "audio_format": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "mp3",
              "flac",
              "wav",
              "wav32",
              "opus",
              "aac"
            ],
            "default": "flac",
            "description": "Output format. **Anneal defaults to flac**; the backend's mp3 is fixed at 128 kbps and audibly lossy."
          },
          "batch_size": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 8,
            "default": 2,
            "description": "Takes per request. Each costs roughly a full generation."
          },
          "bpm": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 30,
            "maximum": 300
          },
          "key_scale": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "F# minor"
          },
          "time_signature": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "2",
              "3",
              "4",
              "6"
            ]
          },
          "vocal_language": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "en"
          },
          "seed": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Set with use_random_seed=false to reproduce a take."
          },
          "use_random_seed": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true
          },
          "inference_steps": {
            "type": "integer",
            "default": 8,
            "description": "Overrides the tier default (8 for draft, 32 for high). Step one carries a ~46s warm-up; each further step is about a second, so more steps are cheaper than they look."
          },
          "thinking": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": true,
            "description": "Run the 5Hz LM planning pass. **Anneal defaults this to true**, unlike the backend. Better structure, ~30s slower."
          },
          "task_type": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "text2music",
              "cover",
              "repaint",
              "lego",
              "extract",
              "complete"
            ],
            "default": "text2music"
          },
          "quality": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "draft",
              "high"
            ],
            "default": "draft",
            "description": "Model tier. `draft` = acestep-v15-turbo, 8 steps, ~68s. `high` = acestep-v15-sft, 50 steps, ~130s, with CFG enabled and DCW disabled as that model requires. Switching tiers restarts the backend and costs one cold load, because only one DiT fits in memory. Call GET /v1/music/tiers for live availability."
          }
        }
      },
      "SpeechRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "input"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "input": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Text to speak."
          },
          "voice": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "af_heart",
            "description": "See GET /v1/voices."
          },
          "response_format": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "wav",
              "mp3",
              "flac",
              "opus",
              "aac"
            ],
            "default": "wav"
          },
          "speed": {
            "type": "number",
            "minimum": 0.5,
            "maximum": 2.0,
            "default": 1.0
          }
        }
      },
      "ImageRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "prompt"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "prompt": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "size": {
            "type": "string",
            "default": "1024x1024",
            "description": "WxH, snapped to a multiple of 16, max ~1536x1536."
          },
          "steps": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 20,
            "default": 4,
            "description": "schnell is distilled for 4 steps."
          },
          "n": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 4,
            "default": 1
          },
          "seed": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "Omit for random. With n>1, seeds increment."
          },
          "response_format": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "b64_json",
              "path"
            ],
            "default": "b64_json"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
